				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1477,
				28
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Implement comprehensive IPC status reporter and service discovery\n\nIntroduce a complete observability subsystem in `Source/IPC/StatusReporter` to bridge the gap between the native Mountain backend and the Sky frontend. This implementation replaces placeholder logic with a robust `Reporter::Struct` aggregator that tracks IPC health, performance metrics, and service lifecycles.\n\nKey additions include:\n- **DTOs:** Define strict serialization shapes for `ComprehensiveStatusReport`, `HealthMonitor`, `ServiceRegistry`, and granular metrics like `PerformanceMetrics` and `MessageStats`.\n- **Health Monitoring:** Implement logic to detect anomalies (latency spikes, queue overflows, connection loss) and calculate a dynamic health score, triggering automatic recovery attempts via `attempt_recovery`.\n- **Service Discovery:** Enable automatic registration and tracking of core services (Editor, ExtensionHost, File, Storage) with dependency mapping and metrics.\n- **Tauri Commands:** Expose the reporting layer via a suite of commands (e.g., `mountain_get_comprehensive_status`, `mountain_start_ipc_status_reporting`, `mountain_discover_services`) allowing the Wind/Sky layers to poll status or initiate background reporting loops.\n- **Event Emission:** Establish periodic Tauri event streams (`ipc-status-report`, `ipc-health-alert`) for real-time telemetry updates in the UI.\n\nThis layer provides the foundational telemetry required for the Feature Parity dashboard and enables self-healing capabilities for the IPC bridge.",
			"SHA": "882dca7e299c9a1df66926622d6030c9a71b9880"
		},
